[size=5][b]Every mod's keybinds in the game's own Key Bindings menu.[/b][/size]

Mods that add keys usually leave them in an input file, in Mod Settings, or both, and many can't be changed in game at all. Mod Keybinds Menu adds a section per mod to Settings > Controls > Key Bindings with every keyboard action your installed mods add, so you can rebind them next to the vanilla keys. Nothing is hardcoded: the list is built from your installed mods each time the game starts.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]One section per mod in Settings > Controls > Key Bindings, for example [i]"Mods: Let There Be Flight"[/i] or [i]"Mods: Stash QoL"[/i], built at startup from the mods you have installed. Add or remove a mod and the sections follow.
[*]Section and action names come from the mod's files, for example [i]"Vehicle Flight Linear Brake"[/i] or [i]"Transfer Max Quantity"[/i].
[*]Keys stay in sync with Mod Settings: if a mod also has its key in Mod Settings, changing it in either menu changes both.
[*]Actions already in the Key Bindings menu (vanilla, or added by mods like No More Hard-coded Keybinds) are not listed twice.
[*]Never changes the game's files or other mods' files, so mods that edit the settings menu keep working.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url] (optional, for keeping keys in sync with mods that also offer them there)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, or extract the archive into the Cyberpunk 2077 game folder. The files go to:
[code]red4ext/plugins/ModKeybindsMenu/ModKeybindsMenu.dll
red4ext/plugins/ModKeybindsMenu/scripts/[/code]

[size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
Remove the [i]red4ext/plugins/ModKeybindsMenu[/i] folder. Optionally delete [i]r6/cache/modkeybinds/[/i]. Nothing is written to your save.

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Only mods that bind keys through the game's input system show up. Hotkeys registered with Cyber Engine Tweaks stay in the CET overlay.
[*]Gamepad-only actions are not listed: the Key Bindings menu is for keyboard and mouse.
[*]A mod that registers its input file late in startup through Input Loader's plugin interface may only appear from the second launch.
[*]Unbinding an entry that has no Mod Settings option resets it to the mod's default key the next time a save loads.
[/list]

[size=4][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Your action shows up if it has a [i]<button id="IK_..." overridableUI="yourActionName" />[/i] in an input file loaded by Input Loader. Nothing else is needed.

For nicer names than the generated ones, ship [i]r6/config/modkeybinds/<YourMod>.json[/i]:
[code]{
  "_section": "Your Mod",
  "yourActionName": "Open Menu"
}[/code]
[i]_section[/i] names the section for every action in that file. Names can also be LocKey#... keys.

[size=4][b]Source[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/kaporli/mod-keybinds-menu]github.com/kaporli/mod-keybinds-menu[/url] (MIT)
